      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "Integrating specific \"neighborhood health indicators\" would almost certainly make the risk divergence between the two applicants more pronounced, pushing Applicant B toward the Medium risk threshold. A robust risk engine should generally assign a weighted importance to both financial merit and environmental factors, but individual financial strength should usually retain a majority weighting. For a fintech engine, I would recommend giving location stability a moderate weight (perhaps 25-35%) to serve as a critical risk modifier, rather than letting it fully override excellent individual creditworthiness.",
